    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1070">

                <pb facs="1311" n="1293" xml:id="pg1293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.61311/6–1146</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-11T19:00:00-04:00">June 11, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. July wheat export program being finally determined. Pis cable whether FonMin considers report contained urtel 325 June 8 changes Urug need for US wheat to extent that July cargo can be
                        foregone.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d1070-f1"/> Urgent demand from famine areas
                    makes US export position extremely difficult.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1070-f1" n="62" xml:id="d1070-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 333, June 13, 1946, 11 a.m., the Ambassador reported that no July
                    cargo from the United States was required (733.35/6–1346).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
